        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**SP03 \u2014 Three tones, one sampled sequence**  \n**Can a 10 Hz spectral peak identify the original tone?** Run **2 s at 64 Hz**; open Scope.  \nAt 64 Hz all three source sequences match; difference is zero. Overlay is intentional: hide channels to inspect each.  \nChange shifted frequency_hz 74 \u2192 70: predict a 6 Hz alias. Restore 74, then run at 256 Hz to distinguish the tones.  \n[Open SP03 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP03-aliasing/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT teaching materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_lec21/) \u00b7 [S7 signal sources](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/SIGNAL_SOURCES.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1241,
          "height": 320,
          "font_size": 18
        }
